      "keyInsight": "Nobody runs an Olympic marathon the very first day they purchase running shoes. If you try, your lungs burn and your knees collapse within five minutes. Yet people attempt that exact stunt with assertiveness. They read half a chapter, march straight into their difficult boss's office, and demand a massive raise. When the meeting goes sideways, they throw up their hands and declare assertiveness a failure. That is not how change operates. Sustainable growth works on a steady ladder of small, low-stakes experiments. You warm up your voice by ordering coffee with extra milk. You practice steady eye contact with the friendly grocery cashier. You build conversational muscle tone where the cost of a mistake is basically zero.",
