      "bookTitle": "The Assertiveness Workbook",
      "author": "Randy J. Paterson",
      "category": "Philosophy",
      "type": "quote",
      "headline": "The Right to Say 'I Do Not Know'",
      "body": "You do not need an instant, brilliant answer for every curveball thrown your way. Owning what you do not know with confidence is vastly more assertive than faking certainty.",
